KZ3 patch 1125 (SPU pass 106): upstream ps3recomp PR #484 by tekulvw (MIT, head 13a7676b), "spu: copy only the
reserved lines of a PUT under the lock-line lock", ported onto KZ3's DMA patches 1026/1056/1065/1121.

A plain PUT whose multi-line span touches a reserved line used to copy the whole span under the lock. Now the lines
that are not reserved are copied first without the lock (as an unreserved span is), then the locked pass copies the
reserved lines it skipped and notifies every reserved line; a line reserved after its unlocked copy is notified but
not copied again (a peer may already have committed on top of it). Single-line spans and spans of 192+ lines keep the
old whole-span locked copy. Adapted: KZ3's lock is patch 1056's stripe set (spu_ll_mask of the span, then
spu_ll_lock_mask) instead of upstream's global spu_lockline_lock, so the locked pass holds the span's stripes only for
the reserved lines' copies. No switch (no behaviour change for a PUT that touches no reserved line).
Test: the PR's test_unaligned_wide_put_around_a_reserved_line in runtime/spu/tests/test_spu_lockline_peer.c
(tools/spu/test_lockline.sh, t_lockline_peer).

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.18.0 (SPU pass 108): ours (stripes); the test file upstream's (#484 merged).

